The look judge of round 1 scored identity 7.0 and proportion 8.0 for both children. It named
three faults for Tom and three for Lily. Green changed only the two asset files. The child base,
the scripts, the tests, the adults, and the preset pin stay as they were.

Tom, the three faults and the fixes:
- The hair was a smooth dome. The hair now carries ten pointed locks: four sweep up to the
  character's left, one cowlick points up to the character's right, one side lock breaks the round
  dome at the top left, one back lock breaks the round mass in the side view, two fringe locks
  sweep over the brow, and two side locks fall in front of the ears. The blend radius is 0.006 m,
  so the locks keep their points.
- The mouth was a closed dark red line. The mouth is now an open toothy smile: a filled mouth
  cavity and a band of teeth, both painted profiles on the face layer. The mouth is 0.104 m wide
  and 0.034 m deep.
- The face lacked defined eyebrows and a rosy cheek blush. The brows are 0.050 m long and 0.019 m
  thick, and each cheek carries a rosy blush of #e8786a over smaller freckles. The blush keeps a
  relative luminance of 0.56, so it stays out of the eye window of the proportion script.

Lily, the three faults and the fixes:
- The shirt had no white collar. The white Peter Pan collar sits at the neckline: a flat ring round
  the neck at 0.640 m with two rounded lobes that hang over the chest at 0.634 m.
- The shoes had no laces and the wrong shape. The red sneakers carry a white toe cap at the front,
  a white sole, and two white lace bands over the instep. Each lace band is the shoe inflated by
  8 mm and cut by a slab of 16 mm, so the band follows the curve of the shoe.
- The skirt was not pleated. The red skirt carries ten pleats. The fold is a radial ripple of
  9 mm, and it starts below the hem of the tee, so the waist keeps a round edge. The ripple uses
  the Lipschitz factor of 1.8, so the distance field keeps its true size and the triangle
  reduction succeeds. The build prints no warning line.

